      "description": "Average time each I/O actually took \u2014 how FAST the disk is, next to how MUCH it is moving. Typically 1-2 ms here, peaking around 4 ms. This replaced a %util panel: util is derived from 'time the queue was non-empty', which was designed for single-queue spinning disks. NVMe has thousands of parallel queues, so util can read 100 % while the device is barely working. Latency stays meaningful.\n\nGaps in the line are periods with no I/O at all (0/0 is dropped rather than drawn as a fake 0 ms) \u2014 a gap means idle, not fast.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
