    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus-homelab"
      },
      "description": "How much data the host is moving, and which way. eno1 is the wired NIC and carries effectively all of it (it holds the default route at metric 100); tailscale0 is the VPN, worth watching because Tailscale Funnel exposes a public URL. Wifi (wlp3s0) is connected but excluded \u2014 it only ever carried broadcast noise. Jellyfin streaming shows as eno1 tx; a docker pull shows as eno1 rx. Transmit is mirrored below the axis.\n\nHost NIC counters come from cAdvisor's root cgroup (id=\"/\"), not node-exporter. node-exporter runs on the homelab bridge, and /proc/net/dev is generated per network namespace \u2014 resolved from the reading process, not from the mount it was reached through. So despite --path.rootfs=/host it only sees its own veth: node_network_* on this host is Prometheus scrape traffic, not host traffic. See monitoring/README.md.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
